;; Lib/test's language-core methods pyi does not run as CPython 3.14.10 does (bin/pyi lib-test, test/python/libtest_judge.ae;
;; queue 194, PY6a), each in a class. :classes: each class's title, kind (:design, by design; :deferred, an owner's
;; work), owner (the milestone whose files it waits on), why, where it was decided, and :match, the regexes the
;; writer classes a new method's line by ("import MESSAGE", "stopped-in MESSAGE", "crash MESSAGE", or pyi's
;; "OUTCOME REASON"). :methods: every method not equal, "MODULE/TEST-ID" -> its class, written by
;; bin/pyi lib-test --record (a method's class kept, else the first class whose :match finds its line; a method of no
;; class is printed, left out and the run exits 3: no placeholder class is written, as CS265 (a) and CS266 (a)'s
;; writers). The judge passes a method that is not equal only when :methods names it with a class of :classes.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:ast-objects
  {:title "compile() to and from AST objects"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY9"
   :why "compile(..., ast.PyCF_ONLY_AST) returns a code object, and compile() of an ast.Module refuses it: _ast's node classes exist (PY6a) but the bridge between Python forms and ast objects is the native reader's (survey §6.6: \"_ast (Python forms <-> ast objects: the bridge that makes ast.parse inside pyi the native reader)\")"
   :decided "survey §6.6, PYS4; the user, 2026-11-03 (PY9 beside PY6)"
   :match [#"^failure <class 'code'> != <class 'ast\.Module'>" #"compile\(\) arg 1 must be a string, bytes or AST object" #"'code' object has no attribute 'body'"]}
